From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:18:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] imx93-cargt-00363-00365: bring u-boot dts in line with
 the kernel dts

Two mismatches against the kernel imx93-cargt-00363-00365.dts:

- TCPCs: the 00365 rev 4 moved U17 to I2C 0x51, so the first PTN5110
  is tcpc@51, and the second one's ALERT is GPIO2_IO10, not IO11. The
  board code already probes 0x51/0x52 by hardcoded address, so this is
  a DT fix rather than a behaviour change for the tcpc setup.
- EQOS PHY reset: the 00365 Ethernet resets are active-low (rev A,
  "Inverted Ethernet reset signals"). U-Boot's eth-phy uclass drives
  the PHY node's reset-gpios, so with ACTIVE_HIGH the "deassert" step
  drove PCA9555 P00 low and left the EQOS PHY held in reset. Fix both
  the &ethphy1 override and snps,reset-gpios.

Also use the kernel's tuned RGMII pad settings for EQOS and FEC: 0x50e
for MDC/MDIO and 0x51e for RGMII, instead of the NXP EVK's 0x57e data
and 0x5fe clocks, so U-Boot networking runs on the drive strength the
board is validated with under Linux.

Backport of meta-imx-cargt wrynose cbd8a96 and 17f8c82 (!56), by Tim
Carney. Its carrier-pwr-en removal is in the patch before this one.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board support]
Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
---
